# What this file holds, and what it does not.
#
# Repository-wide rules only. A component's own build products are ignored by
# that component's own .gitignore, so the rule sits beside the thing it
# describes and travels with it: engine/, lib/, extensions/cmetta/,
# extensions/node/, extensions/python/, extensions/mork/mork_ffi/ and
# examples/ch19-spaces-backed-by-anything/ each carry one. Six blocks lived
# here until 2026-08-28 and named paths four directories away.
#
# Tool caches are absent deliberately and must stay absent: ruff, pytest, mypy,
# Hypothesis and import-linter each write a .gitignore containing `*` INSIDE
# the cache directory they create, which is why none of them has ever appeared
# in `git status`.

*.py[cod]
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# The engine's own dependency directory, where lib/lib_gitimport's `git-import!`
# puts a checkout it fetched at a pinned revision, alongside a .lock per
# dependency. Acquired, never authored.
repos/

# pytest-benchmark's store, the one tool cache that does NOT self-ignore. It is
# empty today and git does not track an empty directory, so the gap stayed
# invisible until the first --benchmark-autosave run wrote into it.
.benchmarks/

# Agent scratch: books, cloned prior art, gate logs, tree copies, working
# ledgers. Never released, and skipped by .codespellrc for the same reason;
# a ledger meant to persist lives at the workspace root outside this repo.
ai-tmp/
ai-*.md
ai-tmp-*

# Browser-automation scratch. Four of these console logs and page snapshots
# were committed by accident on 2026-08-21 as part of an unrelated merge;
# they are session debris, not a deliverable.
.playwright-mcp/

# Jupyter's autosave copies, written beside any notebook it opens. The shipped
# notebook is extensions/python/notebooks/tour.ipynb and the gate re-executes it,
# so a reader who opens it produces these on the first edit.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
